# LaunchKit — Windsurf Rules

You are working on **LaunchKit**, a production-ready Next.js 15 SaaS boilerplate.

## Stack (current — do not deviate)

- **Framework**: Next.js 15 App Router + TypeScript (strict)
- **Database**: Neon Postgres (serverless) + Drizzle ORM — OR — Supabase + Drizzle ORM
- **Auth**: Clerk (multi-tenant, orgs, webhooks) — only provider
- **Billing**: Stripe only (Apple Pay + Google Pay + Link via Checkout) — one-time purchase
- **UI**: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui + Radix primitives
- **AI**: Vercel AI SDK — 11 providers via `getModel()` factory in `lib/ai.ts`
- **Email**: React Email + Resend
- **Monorepo**: Turborepo + pnpm workspaces

## Critical Rules

### TypeScript
- Add `// @ts-nocheck` to ANY file that imports from `@launchkit/database` (Drizzle dual-instance type conflict)
- No `any` without justification, no casting without reason
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions

### Components
- Default to **Server Components** — add `"use client"` only when you need hooks, browser APIs, or event handlers
- Keep client components at leaf level
- Import from `@/components/ui/` for shadcn primitives

### Database
```typescript
// Always import from the package, never raw drizzle-orm in app code
import { db } from "@launchkit/database";
import { users } from "@launchkit/database/schema/users";
import { eq, and, desc } from "drizzle-orm";

const row = await db.select().from(users).where(eq(users.id, id));
```

### Auth (every API route)
```typescript
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server";
const { userId, orgId } = await auth();
if (!userId) return NextResponse.json({ error: "Unauthorized" }, { status: 401 });
```

### AI calls
```typescript
// NEVER instantiate providers directly — always use the factory
import { getModel } from "@/lib/ai";
import { streamText } from "ai";

const result = streamText({ model: getModel("gpt-5.4-mini"), messages });
return result.toDataStreamResponse();
```

### Email
```typescript
import { sendEmail, PurchaseConfirmationEmail } from "@launchkit/email";
await sendEmail({ to: email, subject: "...", react: PurchaseConfirmationEmail({ ... }) });
```

### Routing
- Add new public routes to `publicRoutes[]` in `apps/web/middleware.ts`
- Never bypass middleware for protected routes

## Monorepo Structure

```
apps/web/               → Next.js 15 main app
  app/
    api/                → API routes (always auth-check first)
    dashboard/          → Protected pages
    (marketing)/        → Public landing, pricing, demo, prompts
    portal/             → Post-purchase GitHub access delivery
  components/
    ui/                 → shadcn/ui primitives
    dashboard/          → Sidebar, header
    ai/                 → Chat, image gen, agents
    plugins/            → Feedback, testimonials, roadmap, waitlist
  lib/
    ai.ts               → AI factory (getModel)
    github.ts           → GitHub invite automation
    entitlement.ts      → Purchase verification
  middleware.ts         → Clerk auth + publicRoutes

packages/
  database/             → Drizzle schema + Neon client
  email/                → React Email templates
  storage/              → Multi-provider (Vercel Blob, S3, Supabase)
  create-launchkit/     → CLI tool (npx create-launchkit@latest)
  mcp-server/           → MCP server for AI tool integration
```

## DO NOT
- Use `Lemon Squeezy` — removed from codebase
- Use `Trigger.dev` — removed, use Vercel cron or Next.js route handlers
- Import `@launchkit/database` in client components
- Instantiate AI providers directly (use `getModel()`)
- Create API routes that skip `auth()` for protected resources
- Add `"use client"` to page.tsx files unless absolutely required
